  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1 (Katharine Lee Bates' 1911 text) to Samuel A. Ward's tune 'Materna', transcribed from the 1917 community songbook page scan (No. 5, in C; transcription saved as scores/b8/scan/america_beautiful_1917.ly) and checked note by note. Simplification: the one C sharp (on 'A-' of 'Above the fruited plain') is played as 1 (C). D drum: as written (range 2 to high 3), D minLayout 13. C drum: the C drum has no high 2/3, so the lines 'Above the fruited plain!', 'America! America!', 'God shed his grace on thee,' and 'From sea to shining sea!' are played one octave lower; C minLayout 11. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
}
